      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Coronary perforation is an infrequent but potentially devastating complication of coronary intervention. Treatment of a broad-based perforation usually requires emergent pericardiocentesis and thoracotomy. We present a novel approach to closure of > or = 1 mm diameter perforations using a dual-catheter covered stent technique."},
